@kind(api)

@meta{
  crate: tomet-edit
}

=[ tomet-edit ]

Backend-neutral editable model of a Tomet document.

A tree of nodes that carry opaque ids, attribute maps, marked text and the
layout trivia (whitespace, comments) of the source they came from, plus a
small closed set of edit operations applied one at a time. Its purpose is
to let an application bridge one document to an external editing runtime
-- typically a CRDT -- without this workspace depending on any of them.

Planned surface (nothing here yet):

- the model types;
- `source -> model` and `model -> source`, where an import followed by an

export with no edits is byte-identical;

- edit operations: insert, delete, move, set attribute, edit text;
- validator diagnostics over an edited model, which only report, because

a runtime that merges concurrent edits cannot reject them.

Not here: any CRDT library, and any sync, session or transport code.
